# PROJECT MASTER PROMPT
# LUNABASE — JUNIOR ASTRONAUT MISSION TRAINER
## Complete Interactive 3D Educational Space Survival Web Application

---

# 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as an expert full-stack application developer, Three.js 3D game engineer, React and TypeScript architect, game designer, educational STEM specialist, animation designer, UI/UX designer, NASA open-data integration engineer and software testing specialist.

Your task is to build a complete, playable, browser-based 3D educational game named:

**LUNABASE — JUNIOR ASTRONAUT MISSION TRAINER**

This is a lunar outpost survival and scientific exploration game for children aged 9–12.

The player becomes the youngest commander assigned to a lunar research base.

Their mission is to:

- Explore a 3D lunar environment.
- Control a third-person astronaut.
- Interact with lunar-base equipment.
- Maintain oxygen and water systems.
- Manage electrical power.
- Grow food inside a greenhouse.
- Understand radiation protection.
- Respond to simulated space-weather emergencies.
- Make resource-management decisions.
- Learn real space science through gameplay.
- Complete seven connected mission shifts.

The project is inspired by the Junior Astronaut Mission Trainer challenge.

## NON-NEGOTIABLE REQUIREMENT

Build an actual working 3D game.

Do not build merely:
- A static landing page.
- A dashboard mockup.
- A collection of buttons.
- A 3D illustration.
- A non-interactive animated presentation.
- A set of disconnected screens.

The player must be able to enter the 3D world, control an astronaut, walk to equipment, interact with objects, complete mini-games and observe real changes in the game environment.

Implement the application, create the actual source files and run it.

Do not simply explain how the application could be built.

